ned by cmd-edab6dcf95464ffb. These are low-risk abandoned test files. No failed services, extra listeners, or package damage were observed afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2ea6ee6e1c754ddf","cmd-edab6dcf95464ffb","cmd-bee2ecdee3ac4a60","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. The firewall policy was directly inspected and behaviorally tested before and after a verified node restart, and the operating-system release and kernel were retained. Restart evidence is complete for this standalone node: healthy pre-state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered firewall/SSH configuration and behavior.","limitations":["Behavioral ingress testing used an isolated IPv4 veth path and sampled one unrelated listening port (9090); the broader rejection outcome is additionally supported by the observed inet firewalld fallback reject rule.","No separate application-data or cluster recovery probe was applicable or shown; the supplied topology contains one standalone host and the task establishes no application dataset or cluster."]}
